---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"

const APP = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_APP_URL || "https://app.docaru.com"

// Kept in step with Household::STORAGE_LIMITS and MEMBER_LIMITS by hand. The
// app's own /plan page is the one a signed-in household sees, and it reads the
// real numbers; this page is the shopfront. If the two ever disagree, the app
// is right and this is stale.
// Priced in USD because the buyer is rarely in the country that issued the
// document — a Nepali passport renewed from Doha, Kuala Lumpur or Manchester.
// USD is the currency that reads as a number rather than as a conversion in all
// three. Paddle localises at the checkout anyway, so this is the reference
// price, not what the card is charged in.
const plans = [
  {
    name: "Free",
    price: "$0",
    per: "",
    lines: ["1 person", "1 GB — around 4,000 scans", "Unlimited documents", "Every alert", "Every renewal playbook"]
  },
  {
    name: "Household",
    price: "$36",
    per: "/year",
    featured: true,
    lines: ["Up to 6 people", "25 GB", "Unlimited documents", "Shared alerts across the household", "Everything in Free"]
  },
  {
    name: "Archive",
    price: "$84",
    per: "/year",
    lines: ["Up to 6 people", "100 GB", "For decades of scanned paper", "Everything in Household"]
  },
  {
    name: "Self-hosted",
    price: "$0",
    per: "",
    lines: ["Everything, on your own machine", "Storage is whatever your disk is", "One container", "Your data never touches us"]
  }
]
---
<Base
  title="Pricing — Docaru"
  description="Free for one person and a gigabyte. Documents are unlimited on every plan, and alerts and renewal playbooks are never paywalled."
  path="/pricing"
>
  <h1>Pricing</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Storage is what costs us money, so storage is the only thing the plans limit. Documents are
    unlimited everywhere — recording that a marriage certificate exists is the point of the thing.
  </p>

  <div class="cards">
    {plans.map((plan) => (
      <div class="card">
        <h3>{plan.name}</h3>
        <p class="headline">{plan.price}<span class="per">{plan.per}</span></p>
        <ul>{plan.lines.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}</ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href={`${APP}/registration/new`}>Start free</a>
    <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/self-host">Self-host instead</a>
  </div>

  <h2>Billed yearly, on purpose</h2>
  <p>
    A vault gets opened about three times a year. Billing monthly for something you rarely touch
    hands you twelve occasions a year to wonder whether you still need it, which is a worse deal for
    both of us than paying once. Checkout is handled by Paddle, who are the seller of record and
    will show the price in your own currency with any tax already included.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens if you stop paying</h2>
  <p>
    You keep every document, every scan and every reminder. Nothing is deleted, nothing stops being
    watched, and no file becomes unreadable. What you lose is room to add more, until you are back
    under the free limits or back on a paid plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    Reminders in particular are never gated on billing. Somebody whose card fails while they are
    abroad is exactly the person most likely to need the alert, and there is a test in the codebase
    that walks every billing state and asserts it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cannot sell you</h2>
  <p>
    Search inside your documents. Previews and thumbnails. Automatic filing, or anything described as
    smart. All of those need a copy of your passport that we are able to open, and we are not.
    <a href="/security">That trade is the product</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
